VERSIONS (published Maven Central artifacts, HEAD 200 verified for all three):
  V0 = dolphinscheduler-master + dolphinscheduler-task-api 3.1.8  host :18318  (pre-CVE-2023-49299)
  V1 = dolphinscheduler-master + dolphinscheduler-task-api 3.1.9  host :18319  (CVE-2023-49299 patched; TARGET, incomplete)
  V2 = dolphinscheduler-master + dolphinscheduler-task-api 3.2.1  host :18321  (CVE-2024-23320 patched; negative)
RUNTIME: eclipse-temurin:11-jdk (Nashorn "js" ScriptEngine is JDK-builtin in 11, removed in 15+).
BUILD: multi-stage -- stage `fetch` (curlimages/curl) pulls the jars from repo1.maven.org
(avoids the flaky ports.ubuntu.com ARM apt mirror), stage 2 (temurin:11-jdk) COPYs them and
compiles Server.java against jackson only (reflection into the DS jars -> no compile-time DS dep).

SINK / GUARD LINEAGE (same method across the pair):
  V0 3.1.8 : SwitchTaskUtils has only evaluate() -> raw arbitrary-JS condition runs unsandboxed.
  V1 3.1.9 : CVE-2023-49299 added generateContentWithTaskParams -- empty-params guard AND a
             no-substitution guard (throws IllegalArgumentException "condition is not valid"
             if originContent.equals(content), i.e. NOTHING was substituted from a ${param}
             template). It checks THAT a substitution happened, NOT WHAT it produced -> incomplete.
  V2 3.2.1 : CVE-2024-23320 added a keyword blacklist {java,invoke,new,eval,function,import,\\}
             scanned against the substituted content -> the residual JS is rejected.

